  "rule": "Each 3-cell chevron or L has a tip (apex or corner) and points away from its other two cells. The target is the tip plus 5 steps in that direction. A target on a shape recolours that whole shape 9. Otherwise the target becomes 9, or 1 if two or more shapes target it.",
  "scope": "Three-cell cardinal chevrons or diagonal L pointers mark targets five steps from their tip. Shared background targets become 1; a target on a shape recolours that entire shape 9. Random scenes mix native 16x16 with synthetic 10..30 canvases and all eight directions, optional bands, collisions and shape hits. Exact dimensions, colour and shape count are supported.",
  "constraints": [
    "Read reference geometry: nearest-squared-distance tip and opposite-arm direction agree with the constructor",
